Anteater Chess V1.0 Source Release
Installation Instructions

Prerequisites (Linux):
- GNU Make
- A C11-compatible compiler (gcc 9+ or clang 10+)
- pkg-config
- GTK+ 3 development headers (only required for the GUI build,
  e.g. libgtk-3-dev on Debian/Ubuntu)

1. Extract the source package:
   gtar xvzf Chess_V1.0_src.tar.gz

2. Change to the project directory:
   cd Chess_V1.0_src

3. Build the program:
   make

4. Run the program:
   ./bin/chess

5. Run the test suite:
   make test

Recommended verification command:
- make clean all test
  Rebuild from scratch, run the tests, and leave the executable in bin/

Optional commands:
- make clean
  Remove generated build files while preserving bin/, bin/logs/, bin/tests/
- make tar
  Regenerate Chess_V1.0_src.tar.gz
- make tar-user
  Generate the user/customer package Chess_V1.0.tar.gz
  (requires bin/chess to have been built first and
  doc/Chess_UserManual.pdf to be present)

Runtime logs are written to:
- bin/logs/

For more details see doc/Chess_UserManual.pdf and
doc/Chess_SoftwareSpec.pdf.
